handoff.notes:
# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

One inline-SVG component, `apps/web/src/rank/RankCrest.tsx`, draws a crest for Raisin, the five Grape tiers at III/II/I and Jlorious. The tier art lives in one table, and one function (`divisionEmbellishment`) sets the division embellishment the same way in every tier. Pips and placements show as a pip bar beside the crest, and Jlorious prints its position and shimmers unless motion is reduced. The crest is `role="img"`, with `aria-label` and `title` equal to `rankWords`/`badgeWords`. Crests appear at every rank on the leaderboard, the account, the match bar (desktop and phone) and Play, with short words beside them in place of the raw strings.

## Files to touch

| Path | | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/rank/RankCrest.tsx` | new | `RankCrest`, `CREST_SIZE_PX`, `divisionEmbellishment`, `TIER_ART` |
| `apps/web/src/rank/rankCrest.css` | new | layout, pip bar, shimmer, reduced motion |
| `apps/web/src/rank/RankCrest.test.tsx` | new | crest tests |
| `apps/web/src/rank/rank.ts` | change | new `rankCaption`; `rankShortWords` drops pips, placements and position |
| `apps/web/src/rank/rank.test.ts` | change | caption and short-words tests |
| `apps/web/src/routes/leaderboard.tsx` | change | four crest sites |
| `apps/web/src/routes/leaderboard.test.tsx` | change | two assertions, one new test |
| `apps/web/src/routes/account.tsx` | change | rank line, badges |
| `apps/web/src/routes/account.test.tsx` | change | rank test |
| `apps/web/src/routes/match.tsx` | change | both rank spans |
| `apps/web/src/routes/match.test.tsx` | change | full/compact test |
| `apps/web/src/routes/play.tsx` | change | `RankPanel` |
| `apps/web/src/routes/play.test.tsx` | change | R661 assertions |
| `apps/web/src/i18n/zh-CN.json` | change | `"Season best: {badges}"` becomes `"Season best:"`; two dead keys go |
| `apps/web/README.md` | change | the `routes/leaderboard.tsx` entry names `RankCrest.tsx` |

Do not touch: `crates/`, `apps/web/src/net/api.ts`, `spec/`, `BUILD.md`, `e2e/`, `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`. Also leave alone `apps/web/src/game/board.css` (`test/ux/board-ux.test.tsx` pins its `.match-ranks` rules) and `apps/web/src/routes/lobby.css` (the Play hub's layout, R1578000).

Governing: SPEC §9.12, R605, R607, R608, R612, R661, R1578000 (Play fits one screen) and R711000 (i18n). No new ruling: the change is presentation only, and R612's words stay as each crest's name and tooltip.

## Steps

1. **`apps/web/src/rank/rank.ts`.** After `rankShortWords`, add:
   ```ts
   /** The words beside a crest (#1650): the tier and its division numeral, or the tier alone for Raisin and Jlorious. The crest draws the pips, placements and position. */
   export function rankCaption(rank: VisibleRank | PeakBadge): string {
     if (rank.tier === "raisin" || rank.tier === "jlorious") return tierName(rank.tier);
     return `${tierName(rank.tier)} ${divisionNumeral(rank.division)}`;
   }
   ```
   - Replace `rankShortWords`'s body with the same two lines, using `tierShortName`. Keep its `rank: VisibleRank` signature.
   - Its doc becomes "`rankCaption` without "Grape", for the phone's rank line beside the crest."
   - Its `t("Raisin {played}/{games}")` and `t("{tier} {division} {pips}/{total}")` calls go.
   - In the header comment, add the Play screen to the users and add "`RankCrest.tsx` draws these ranks as crests (#1650)".

2. **`apps/web/src/rank/rankCrest.css`** (new). Start with a header comment like `game/lock.css`'s: the crest's layout, pip bar and Jlorious shimmer (#1650). Then add these rules, one declaration per line as the repo's CSS is written:
   ```css
   .rank-crest { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 3px; vertical-align: middle; line-height: 1; }
   .rank-crest__art { flex: none; }
   .rank-crest__position { font-weight: 700; }
   .rank-crest__pips { display: inline-flex; gap: 2px; }
   .rank-crest__pip { width: 4px; height: 4px; border: 1px solid currentcolor; border-radius: 50%; opacity: 0.6; }
   .rank-crest__pip[data-filled="true"] { background: currentcolor; opacity: 1; }
   .rank-crest[data-size="large"] .rank-crest__pip { width: 7px; height: 7px; }
   .rank-crest__shimmer { opacity: 0; animation: rank-crest-shimmer 2.4s ease-in-out infinite; }
   @keyframes rank-crest-shimmer { 0%, 100% { opacity: 0; } 50% { opacity: 0.35; } }
   ```
   End the file with this block, preceded by a comment that `index.css` already stops the shimmer under the settings panel's Reduce motion switch:
   ```css
   @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
     .rank-crest__shimmer {
       animation: none;
     }
   }
   ```

3. **`apps/web/src/rank/RankCrest.tsx`** (new).
   - **Header:** cite #1650, §9.12, R605, R607, R608 and R612. Say it is presentation only (CLAUDE.md rule 7), reads only `VisibleRank`/`PeakBadge`, and never sees a rating.
   - **Imports:**
     - `type ReactElement` from `react`
     - `useOsReducedMotion` from `../game/useOsReducedMotion.ts`
     - `t` from `../i18n/i18n.ts`
     - types `GrapeTier`, `PeakBadge`, `VisibleRank` from `../net/api.ts`
     - `useSetting` from `../settings/index.ts`
     - `badgeWords`, `divisionNumeral`, `rankWords`, `tierName` from `./rank.ts`
     - `"./rankCrest.css"`
   - **Constants:**
   ```ts
   export type RankCrestSize = "small" | "large";
   /** A crest's edge in CSS px: small for rows and the phone's rank line, large for the profile, Play and the ladder's own standing. */
   export const CREST_SIZE_PX: Readonly<Record<RankCrestSize, number>> = { small: 16, large: 32 };
   export type RankCrestProps =
     | { rank: VisibleRank; size: RankCrestSize }
     | { badge: PeakBadge; size: RankCrestSize }
     | { tier: GrapeTier; division?: number; size: RankCrestSize }; // the ladder's headings and rows, which carry no pipsPerDivision
   /** Studs per Grape division: one more at each step from III to I, in every tier. */
   const DIVISION_STUDS: Readonly<Record<number, number>> = { 3: 1, 2: 2, 1: 3 };
   /** The one division rule (#1650): the studs, and one inner frame line fewer. */
   export function divisionEmbellishment(division: number | null): { studs: number; frameLines: number } {
     const studs = division === null ? 0 : (DIVISION_STUDS[division] ?? 0);
     return { studs, frameLines: Math.max(0, studs - 1) };
   }
   const SHIELD = "M32 6 L54 14 V32 C54 46 44 54 32 58 C20 54 10 46 10 32 V14 Z";
   /** Berry centres, rows from the point upward: 1, 2, 3 and 4 berries. */
   const BERRY_ROWS: readonly (readonly (readonly [number, number])[])[] = [[[32, 42]], [[27, 34], [37, 34]], [[22, 26], [32, 26], [42, 26]], [[17, 18], [27, 18], [37, 18], [47, 18]]];
   const STUD_Y = 51;
   const STUD_GAP = 6;
   const STUD_R = 2;
   const FRAME_LINE_STEP = 0.1;
   const LEAF_GREEN = "#5f8f3a";
   const LEAVES = [{ cx: 25, cy: 11, rx: 6, ry: 2.5, transform: "rotate(-25 25 11)" }, { cx: 39, cy: 11, rx: 6, ry: 2.5, transform: "rotate(25 39 11)" }];
   const VINES = ["M12 50 C6 40 6 24 12 16", "M52 50 C58 40 58 24 52 16"];
   const WINGS: Readonly<Record<"none" | "small" | "full", readonly string[]>> = {
     none: [],
     small: ["M10 20 C2 16 1 30 4 36 C6 31 8 29 10 31 Z", "M54 20 C62 16 63 30 60 36 C58 31 56 29 54 31 Z"],
     full: ["M10 16 C1 10 0 34 2 44 C5 37 7 35 10 37 Z", "M54 16 C63 10 64 34 62 44 C59 37 57 35 54 37 Z"],
   };
   const CROWN = "M22 9 L24 1 L28 6 L32 0 L36 6 L40 1 L42 9 Z";
   const RAY_COUNT = 8;
   const RAY_LENGTH = 31;
   const RAYS = Array.from({ length: RAY_COUNT }, (_, i) => (i * 2 * Math.PI) / RAY_COUNT).map((a) => [32 + RAY_LENGTH * Math.cos(a), 32 + RAY_LENGTH * Math.sin(a)] as const);
   ```
   - **The art type:** `type TierArt = { frame: string; edge: string; edgeWidth: number; dash: string | undefined; grape: string; berry: number; rows: number; opacity: number; leaves: boolean; vine: boolean; gloss: boolean; halo: boolean; wings: keyof typeof WINGS; glow: string | null; crown: boolean; rays: boolean; shimmer: boolean }`.
